Source: libretech-wiring-tool
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Da Xue <da@libre.computer>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               device-tree-compiler,
               gcc,
               make,
               python3
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/libre-computer-project/libretech-wiring-tool
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libre-computer-gpio
Architecture: all
Depends: gpiod, ${misc:Depends}
Breaks: libretech-gpio (<< ${binary:Version})
Replaces: libretech-gpio (<< ${binary:Version})
Description: Libre Computer header GPIO lookup and control (lgpio)
 Translates 40-pin header pin numbers and BCM (RPi) GPIO numbers to
 chip/line, sysfs, pad, and schematic names for Libre Computer boards.
 Includes get/set helpers for interactive use (not a high-performance API).
 .
 Board data lives under /opt/librecomputer/libretech-wiring-tool/libre-computer/.

Package: libre-computer-dtoverlay
Architecture: all
Depends: device-tree-compiler,
         libre-computer-gpio (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: i2c-tools,
            spi-tools
Breaks: libretech-dtoverlay (<< ${binary:Version})
Replaces: libretech-dtoverlay (<< ${binary:Version})
Description: Libre Computer device-tree overlays and ldto tool
 Compiles and installs per-board device-tree overlays (.dtbo) for header
 buses and accessories (I2C, SPI, UART, PWM, displays, etc.), plus the
 ldto CLI to apply overlays at runtime (configfs) or merge them into the
 EFI/boot DTB for the next boot.
 .
 Board overlays and H40P_* alias maps live under
 /opt/librecomputer/libretech-wiring-tool/libre-computer/.

Package: libretech-gpio
Architecture: all
Section: oldlibs
Depends: libre-computer-gpio (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: transitional package for libre-computer-gpio
 The Libre Computer GPIO tool (lgpio) is now libre-computer-gpio. This
 package pulls it in and can be removed.

Package: libretech-dtoverlay
Architecture: all
Section: oldlibs
Depends: libre-computer-dtoverlay (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: transitional package for libre-computer-dtoverlay
 The Libre Computer device-tree overlays and ldto are now
 libre-computer-dtoverlay. This package pulls it in and can be removed.
